1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308459 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e5/e5c236defa66a00f12cd338ed0012cf91e4d7c15aa4865fc2b1edf5b0e2ea1da.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above.\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}.\n\nFinally, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector {{field-9}} as they move away from the origin, the dominant eigenvalue is \n{{field-10}}.\n\nTherefore,\n{{field-11}} \n$>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b5a36f6-c7fc-5f39-8a18-1389505413c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308459 #edb/ref 1074 "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/97/97f7eb1fbddcd9d927447978efd4c42e705d6835bf0cc74525d42ded8c35346b.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/ed/edc697ab38ae9a56d46181e0a45982b7045224de0cc3c4a786ddbc515f22196c.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}>0.$\n\nSo, for this particular system, both eigenvalues are positive. The dominant eigenvalue is the one with the greatest magnitude.\n\nNow, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ${v}_{1}$ as they move away from the origin, the dominant eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\n\nTherefore, ${\\lambda }_{1}>{\\lambda }_{2}>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n{{field-1}} is {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca7ddbc3-cff0-528a-94e0-d6fbf22a4ad5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308481 #edb/ref 1074 "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/a0/a09d50fa36b2748fb1c65ed16e20d950afbbabc18884ff8718cf1571c4e13b0e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333643" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c833496-a809-5eea-acb1-bfc822315c03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308483 #edb/ref 1074 "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-2x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-2x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/45/450d43a4cbf6dad8d54edbb66fc4a6e44e491290e1dc5d1303057fb0eb7928a7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186422020 #edb/ref 1080 "{v}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422020 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422020 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "065efdb1-4ae6-597a-a0e1-aae8bc0611d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422021 #edb/ref 1080 "y=-x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c7c5dd4-985b-5405-bb39-51253042d52c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422022 #edb/ref 1080 "{v}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422022 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422022 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c90deb3-1281-549a-b9ec-dd098c7da22e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422023 #edb/ref 1080 "a stable node (sink)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422023 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422023 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "116aa627-74f3-55db-9c3e-276499470af8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422025 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422025 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1218b74d-f298-501a-8fba-a0cc4cae244d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422027 #edb/ref 1080 "a stable" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422027 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422027 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14bc55e1-31d7-5798-9f51-9e810ae5b145" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422031 #edb/ref 1080 "infinity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422031 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186422031 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17a445c5-3735-5229-8adb-2046539a15fc" #edb/ref 1759218604